github_url: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/issues/49"
body: "**Found by running the command against a real TODO file in a fresh, default workspace** — no unusual configuration involved.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```bash\npm init td && pm install pm-todos\nprintf \"# TODO\\n\\n- [x] Finished work that must not be lost\\n- [ ] Pending work\\n\" > TODO.md\n\npm todos import TODO.md; echo \"EXIT=$?\"\npm list --status all\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\nEXIT=0\nimported: 1\n - open | Pending work\n```\n\nThe completed item is **gone**. `Finished work that must not be lost` was never created, and the command reported success.\n\n## What happens\n\nstderr carries the cause, once per completed line:\n\n```\nTODO.md:3: create failed — Error: Close reason text is required because\ngovernance.require_close_reason is enabled\n```\n\nThe importer creates each item and, for a checked box, closes it — without supplying a close reason. `governance.require_close_reason` is a **built-in default**: it does not appear in a freshly written `.agents/pm/settings.json`, so this is the out-of-the-box path, not an opted-in strict mode.\n\n## Why this is worse than a failed import\n\nThree properties compound:\n\n1. **It is the normal case.** A TODO file exists to track work; some of it is done. A file with no `[x]` lines is the unusual one.\n2. **The import is partial, not refused.** Pending items are created, completed ones are dropped, and the workspace is left half-converted — the tracker and the file now disagree, and nothing records which lines were lost.\n3. **Exit code 0.** Any agent or script that runs the import and checks the exit status sees success. The failure exists only in stderr text next to output that otherwise reads as a normal run.\n\nThe item dropped is specifically the record of **finished work**, which is the part a user cannot reconstruct by looking at what is left.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nThe close needs a reason. The natural one is available at the call site — the source line — so something like:\n\n```ts\nawait client.close(id, \"closed\", {\n  message: \"Import completed TODO item\",\n  resolution: `Imported as completed from ${file}:${lineNumber}`,\n});\n```\n\nWhatever text is chosen, two things matter beyond it:\n\n- **Do not exit 0 on a partial import.** Either refuse the whole file before writing anything, or exit non-zero and name the lines that were dropped. A partial write reported as success is the part that turns a fixable bug into lost data.\n- Worth checking `todos sync` for the same path, since it also reconciles completed state, and `todos export` for the inverse.\n\n## Environment\n\n`pm-todos` current `main`, `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.8.6/2026.8.7, fresh `pm init` workspace, Linux."
